    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both of its tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI converted owner deletion from a hard delete to a soft delete:\n\n**`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\")`) initialized to `false`, with getter/setter, so a newly created owner is not deleted.\n\n**Database schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `deleted` column defaulting to `FALSE`. This matters because tests run under the hsqldb profile with `ddl-auto=none`; the `DEFAULT FALSE` also keeps the pre-seeded owner rows (which omit the column) as not-deleted.\n\n**OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` response schema (not `OwnerFields`, so it isn't a create input). MapStruct maps it automatically since the names match, so `GET` responses now include `deleted`.\n\n**Controller** (`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- `deleteOwner` now sets `deleted = true`, saves the owner (retaining the row), and returns `200 OK` with the owner body instead of removing the record.\n- `rejectDuplicateIdentity` (household/identity check) and `assignPossibleDuplicate` (soft-duplicate check) now skip owners flagged deleted via a new `isDeleted` helper, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains`, `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`) and the full build pass.\n\nI did not touch the V2 controller \u2014 it only exposes `/v2/owners` listing and has no delete operation.",
